GEOS thirdPartyLibs 9b55672f6f8a73d02fd632396eb0410e58c9b120 (TPL tag 361-1070) -- superlu_dist URL hash typo

Class: build-system compatibility fix (no source/algorithm change).
Problem: CMakeLists.txt sets SUPERLU_URL_HASH to a 65-character string
("...a2edf58a"); a SHA-256 has 64 hex characters, so ExternalProject's
URL_HASH check can never succeed and the superlu_dist download step fails
("does not match expected value ... Each download failed!").  The tarball
https://github.com/xiaoyeli/superlu_dist/archive/0f6efc3.tar.gz actually
downloaded on 2026-09-05 has sha256
49cd47da22fe72a37011e8dfaf94bd63ad8d61cc8144eac7a571bcbd0a2edf58, i.e. the
upstream string minus its trailing extra "a".  The same 65-character string is
still present on upstream master (checked 2026-09-05); upstream CI evidently
builds superlu_dist from a pre-populated mirror, not through this hash.
Fix: drop the trailing character.  Impact: none on the built code; the hash now
verifies the very tarball upstream intended.  Verified: TPL superbuild proceeds
past the superlu_dist download.
Applied by level3/geos/build.sh (git apply, idempotent); recorded in the
profile fingerprint.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index ab7fe24..9a6ecac 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -851,7 +851,7 @@ list(APPEND build_list metis )
 if( ENABLE_MPI AND ENABLE_SUPERLU_DIST )
   set(SUPERLU_DIR "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/superlu_dist")
   set(SUPERLU_URL "https://github.com/xiaoyeli/superlu_dist/archive/0f6efc3.tar.gz")
-  set(SUPERLU_URL_HASH "49cd47da22fe72a37011e8dfaf94bd63ad8d61cc8144eac7a571bcbd0a2edf58a")
+  set(SUPERLU_URL_HASH "49cd47da22fe72a37011e8dfaf94bd63ad8d61cc8144eac7a571bcbd0a2edf58")
 
   if ( CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "Clang" AND CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_VERSION VERSION_GREATER 16.0 )
     set(SUPERLU_C_FLAGS "-fPIC ${C_FLAGS_NO_WARNINGS}")
